IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `act-nouns`

-- Legislation Act 2001 (Australian Capital Territory), chapter 14: Interpretation of Acts and statutory instruments (Parts 14.1 and 14.2).
--
-- The chapter gives guidance on working out the meaning of an Act (s 137 (1)): prefer the interpretation that best achieves the Act's purpose (s 139),
-- read the provisions in the context of the whole Act (s 140), and say what material outside the Act may be considered (ss 141 to 143).
-- The judgements the chapter leaves to the reader (which interpretation best achieves the purpose, whether material is relevant) are plain inputs.
-- s 137 (1) and (2) state the purpose and the limit of the chapter and create no rule; the coverage table records them as not operative.
--
-- A rule that says a thing "may" or "must" be done answers JUST TRUE when its conditions are met, and NOTHING otherwise.
-- A rule that says a thing "does not" or "is not" answers JUST FALSE where its condition holds.
-- A "means" definition answers TRUE or FALSE.

§ `Legislation Act 2001 (ACT): chapter 14, Interpretation of Acts and statutory instruments`

§§ `Part 14.1: Purpose and scope`

-- src:1770 | In this chapter:
-- src:1771 | Act includes a statutory instrument.
-- src:1772 | Note Section 7 (3) provides that a reference to an Act includes a reference to a provision of an Act. Section 13 (3) provides that a reference to a statutory instrument includes a reference to a provision of a statutory instrument.
@ref s 136 (src:1770-1772)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of Act or instrument`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 136: the kind of document is an Act for chapter 14` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an Act` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a subordinate law` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a disallowable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a notifiable instrument` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a commencement notice` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory instrument of another kind` THEN JUST TRUE

-- s 137 (3) and (4): the common law presumption operates with the chapter, whether it came into existence before or after the chapter commenced.
-- src:1777 | (3) In particular, this chapter assumes that common law presumptions operate in conjunction with this chapter.
@ref s 137 (3) (src:1777-1777)
-- src:1778 | (4) Subsection (3) also applies to common law presumptions that come into existence after the commencement of this chapter.
@ref s 137 (4) (src:1778-1778)
GIVEN theCommonLawPresumptionExists IS A BOOLEAN, theCommonLawPresumptionCameIntoExistenceAfterTheChapterCommenced IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 137 (3), (4): the common law presumption operates in conjunction with chapter 14` MEANS
    IF   theCommonLawPresumptionExists
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Part 14.2: Key principles of interpretation`

-- src:1783 | In this part:
-- src:1784 | working out the meaning of an Act means—
-- src:1785 | (a) resolving an ambiguous or obscure provision of the Act; or
-- src:1786 | (b) confirming or displacing the apparent meaning of the Act; or
-- src:1787 | (c) finding the meaning of the Act when its apparent meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable; or
-- src:1788 | (d) finding the meaning of the Act in any other case.
@ref s 138 (src:1783-1788)
GIVEN theTaskIsResolvingAnAmbiguousOrObscureProvisionOfTheAct IS A BOOLEAN, theTaskIsConfirmingOrDisplacingTheApparentMeaningOfTheAct IS A BOOLEAN, theTaskIsFindingTheMeaningOfTheActWhenItsApparentMeaningLeadsToAResultThatIsManifestlyAbsurdOrUnreasonable IS A BOOLEAN, theTaskIsFindingTheMeaningOfTheActInAnyOtherCase IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 138: the task is working out the meaning of an Act` MEANS
    theTaskIsResolvingAnAmbiguousOrObscureProvisionOfTheAct
    OR theTaskIsConfirmingOrDisplacingTheApparentMeaningOfTheAct
    OR theTaskIsFindingTheMeaningOfTheActWhenItsApparentMeaningLeadsToAResultThatIsManifestlyAbsurdOrUnreasonable
    OR theTaskIsFindingTheMeaningOfTheActInAnyOtherCase

-- Which interpretation best achieves the purpose of the Act is a judgement the text leaves to the reader.
-- src:1791 | (1) In working out the meaning of an Act, the interpretation that would best achieve the purpose of the Act is to be preferred to any other interpretation.
@ref s 139 (1) (src:1791-1791)
GIVEN theTaskIsWorkingOutTheMeaningOfAnAct IS A BOOLEAN, theInterpretationWouldBestAchieveThePurposeOfTheAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 139 (1): the interpretation is to be preferred to any other interpretation` MEANS
    IF   theTaskIsWorkingOutTheMeaningOfAnAct AND theInterpretationWouldBestAchieveThePurposeOfTheAct
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The section applies whether or not the purpose is expressly stated, so both answers of the input give TRUE.
-- src:1792 | (2) This section applies whether or not the Act’s purpose is expressly stated in the Act.
-- src:1793 | Note The Human Rights Act 2004, s 30 (which is about interpreting legislation to be consistent with human rights) is also relevant to interpreting territory laws.
@ref s 139 (2) (src:1792-1793)
GIVEN thePurposeOfTheActIsExpresslyStatedInTheAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 139 (2): section 139 applies` MEANS
    IF   thePurposeOfTheActIsExpresslyStatedInTheAct
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE TRUE

-- src:1796 | In working out the meaning of an Act, the provisions of the Act must be read in the context of the Act as a whole.
-- src:1797 | Examples
-- src:1798 | 1 The long title of an Act provides that it is an Act to give certain benefits to the holders of pensioner cards. Section 4 provides ‘This Act applies to a holder of a pensioner card’. Section 22 provides that the commissioner may grant ‘a person’ an exemption from payment of rates. The Act does not contain a definition of ‘person’. Section 22 must be read in the context of the Act as a whole so that the commissioner may only grant exemptions to people who are holders of pensioner cards.
-- src:1799 | 2 The Drug Testing Regulation 2001 (made under the Drug Testing Act 2000 (hypothetical)), s 6 contains the following heading:
-- src:1800 | 6 Corresponding law—Act, s 100, def corresponding law
-- src:1801 | The heading indicates that the section has been made for the definition of corresponding law in the Drug Testing Act 2000, s 100.
-- src:1802 | 3 Section 12 (1) of a subordinate law refers to ‘a non-conviction order under the Crimes (Sentencing) Act 2005’. No other kind of order is mentioned in the section and the word ‘order’ is not otherwise defined in the subordinate law. Subsections (2), (4), (7) and (9) of the same section, which only refer to ‘the order’, are to be understood as referring to the order mentioned in s (1).
-- src:1803 | Note See s 126 and s 127 for material that is, or is not, part of an Act or statutory instrument.
@ref s 140 (src:1796-1803)
GIVEN theTaskIsWorkingOutTheMeaningOfAnAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 140: the provisions of the Act must be read in the context of the Act as a whole` MEANS
    IF   theTaskIsWorkingOutTheMeaningOfAnAct
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1806 | (1) In working out the meaning of an Act, material not forming part of the Act may be considered.
-- src:1807 | Note 1 See s 146 for the meaning of may and must.
-- src:1808 | Note 2 See s 126 and s 127 for material that is, or is not, part of an Act or statutory instrument.
-- src:1809 | Note 3 See s 142 for material that may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act or statutory instrument.
@ref s 141 (1) (src:1806-1809)
GIVEN theTaskIsWorkingOutTheMeaningOfAnAct IS A BOOLEAN, theMaterialFormsPartOfTheAct IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141 (1): the material may be considered` MEANS
    IF   theTaskIsWorkingOutTheMeaningOfAnAct AND (NOT theMaterialFormsPartOfTheAct)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The matters are listed as the text prints them, each with its paragraph letter.
-- src:1810 | (2) In deciding whether material not forming part of an Act should be considered in working out the meaning of the Act, and the weight to be given to the material, the following matters must be taken into account:
-- src:1811 | (a) the desirability of being able to rely on the ordinary meaning of the Act, having regard to the purpose of the Act and the provisions of the Act read in the context of the Act as a whole;
-- src:1812 | (b) the undesirability of prolonging proceedings without compensating advantage;
-- src:1813 | (c) the accessibility of the material to the public.
@ref s 141 (2) (src:1810-1813)
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 141 (2): the matters that must be taken into account` MEANS
    LIST
        "(a) the desirability of being able to rely on the ordinary meaning of the Act, having regard to the purpose of the Act and the provisions of the Act read in the context of the Act as a whole;"
        , "(b) the undesirability of prolonging proceedings without compensating advantage;"
        , "(c) the accessibility of the material to the public."

-- src:1814 | (3) Subsection (2) does not limit the matters that may be taken into account.
@ref s 141 (3) (src:1814-1814)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141 (3): subsection (2) limits the matters that may be taken into account` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1815 | (4) For subsection (2) (c), material in the register is taken to be accessible to the public.
-- src:1816 | Note The register is the ACT legislation register (see dict, pt 2, def register).
@ref s 141 (4) (src:1815-1816)
GIVEN theMaterialIsInTheRegister IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141 (4): the material is taken to be accessible to the public for subsection (2) (c)` MEANS
    IF   theMaterialIsInTheRegister
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- Table 142: the seven kinds of material, in the order of the table.
-- src:1822 | Table 142
-- src:1824 | | column 1 item | column 2 Act | column 3 statutory instrument |
-- src:1825 | | 1 | material not forming part of the Act contained in an authorised version of the Act Note See ch 3 (Authorised versions and evidence of laws and legislative material). | material not forming part of the statutory instrument contained in an authorised version of the instrument Note See ch 3 (Authorised versions and evidence of laws and legislative material). |
-- src:1826 | | 2 | any relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the Act was passed | any relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity that was presented to the Legislative Assembly— (a) if the statutory instrument was presented to the Assembly—before the end of 6 sitting days after the day the instrument was presented to the Assembly; or (b) in any other case—before the instrument was made |
-- src:1827 | | 3 | any relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly that was made to the Assembly before the Act was passed | any relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly that was made to the Assembly— (a) if the statutory instrument was presented to the Assembly—before the end of 6 sitting days after the day the instrument was presented to the Assembly; or (b) in any other case—before the instrument was made |
-- src:1828 | | 4 | any explanatory statement (however described) for the bill that became the Act, or any other relevant document, that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the Act was passed | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly—any explanatory statement (however described) for the instrument, or any other relevant document, that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the end of 6 sitting days after the instrument was presented to the Assembly |
-- src:1829 | | 5 | the presentation speech made to the Legislative Assembly during the passage of the bill that became the Act | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly by a member of the Assembly—any presentation speech made to the Assembly |
-- src:1830 | | 6 | official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly in relation to the bill that became the Act | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly—official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly in relation to the statutory instrument |
-- src:1831 | | 7 | any relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party | any relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party |
@ref table 142 (src:1822-1831)
DECLARE `Material in table 142` IS ONE OF
    `item 1: material not forming part of the Act or instrument, contained in an authorised version of it`
    `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity`
    `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly`
    `item 4: an explanatory statement, or other relevant document`
    `item 5: a presentation speech`
    `item 6: official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly`
    `item 7: a relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party`

-- Column 2 (an Act): items 2 to 6 need that the material was presented or made before the Act was passed.
-- "The material is as the item describes it" takes the judgement "relevant" that items 2, 3, 4 and 7 use as an input.
-- src:1819 | (1) In working out the meaning of an Act, material mentioned in table 142, column 2 may be considered.
@ref s 142 (1) (src:1819-1819)
-- src:1822 | Table 142
-- src:1824 | | column 1 item | column 2 Act | column 3 statutory instrument |
-- src:1825 | | 1 | material not forming part of the Act contained in an authorised version of the Act Note See ch 3 (Authorised versions and evidence of laws and legislative material). | material not forming part of the statutory instrument contained in an authorised version of the instrument Note See ch 3 (Authorised versions and evidence of laws and legislative material). |
-- src:1826 | | 2 | any relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the Act was passed | any relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity that was presented to the Legislative Assembly— (a) if the statutory instrument was presented to the Assembly—before the end of 6 sitting days after the day the instrument was presented to the Assembly; or (b) in any other case—before the instrument was made |
-- src:1827 | | 3 | any relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly that was made to the Assembly before the Act was passed | any relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly that was made to the Assembly— (a) if the statutory instrument was presented to the Assembly—before the end of 6 sitting days after the day the instrument was presented to the Assembly; or (b) in any other case—before the instrument was made |
-- src:1828 | | 4 | any explanatory statement (however described) for the bill that became the Act, or any other relevant document, that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the Act was passed | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly—any explanatory statement (however described) for the instrument, or any other relevant document, that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the end of 6 sitting days after the instrument was presented to the Assembly |
-- src:1829 | | 5 | the presentation speech made to the Legislative Assembly during the passage of the bill that became the Act | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly by a member of the Assembly—any presentation speech made to the Assembly |
-- src:1830 | | 6 | official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly in relation to the bill that became the Act | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly—official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly in relation to the statutory instrument |
-- src:1831 | | 7 | any relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party | any relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party |
@ref table 142, column 2 (src:1822-1831)
GIVEN item IS A `Material in table 142`, theMaterialIsAsTheItemDescribesIt IS A BOOLEAN, theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheActWasPassed IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142 (1): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act` MEANS
    IF   NOT theMaterialIsAsTheItemDescribesIt
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER item
         WHEN `item 1: material not forming part of the Act or instrument, contained in an authorised version of it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity` THEN
             IF   theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheActWasPassed
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly` THEN
             IF   theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheActWasPassed
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 4: an explanatory statement, or other relevant document` THEN
             IF   theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheActWasPassed
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 5: a presentation speech` THEN
             IF   theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheActWasPassed
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 6: official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly` THEN
             IF   theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheActWasPassed
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 7: a relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party` THEN JUST TRUE

-- Column 3 (a statutory instrument).
-- "Before the end of 6 sitting days after the day the instrument was presented" is read as: the material was presented or made on or before the 6th sitting day after that day.
-- The input counts the sitting days from 1, the first sitting day after the day the instrument was presented.
-- src:1820 | (2) In working out the meaning of a statutory instrument, material mentioned in table 142, column 3 may be considered.
@ref s 142 (2) (src:1820-1820)
-- src:1822 | Table 142
-- src:1824 | | column 1 item | column 2 Act | column 3 statutory instrument |
-- src:1825 | | 1 | material not forming part of the Act contained in an authorised version of the Act Note See ch 3 (Authorised versions and evidence of laws and legislative material). | material not forming part of the statutory instrument contained in an authorised version of the instrument Note See ch 3 (Authorised versions and evidence of laws and legislative material). |
-- src:1826 | | 2 | any relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the Act was passed | any relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity that was presented to the Legislative Assembly— (a) if the statutory instrument was presented to the Assembly—before the end of 6 sitting days after the day the instrument was presented to the Assembly; or (b) in any other case—before the instrument was made |
-- src:1827 | | 3 | any relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly that was made to the Assembly before the Act was passed | any relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly that was made to the Assembly— (a) if the statutory instrument was presented to the Assembly—before the end of 6 sitting days after the day the instrument was presented to the Assembly; or (b) in any other case—before the instrument was made |
-- src:1828 | | 4 | any explanatory statement (however described) for the bill that became the Act, or any other relevant document, that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the Act was passed | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly—any explanatory statement (however described) for the instrument, or any other relevant document, that was presented to the Legislative Assembly before the end of 6 sitting days after the instrument was presented to the Assembly |
-- src:1829 | | 5 | the presentation speech made to the Legislative Assembly during the passage of the bill that became the Act | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly by a member of the Assembly—any presentation speech made to the Assembly |
-- src:1830 | | 6 | official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly in relation to the bill that became the Act | if the statutory instrument was presented to the Legislative Assembly—official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly in relation to the statutory instrument |
-- src:1831 | | 7 | any relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party | any relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party |
@ref table 142, column 3 (src:1822-1831)
GIVEN item IS A `Material in table 142`, theMaterialIsAsTheItemDescribesIt IS A BOOLEAN, theInstrumentWasPresentedToTheAssembly IS A BOOLEAN, theInstrumentWasPresentedToTheAssemblyByAMemberOfTheAssembly IS A BOOLEAN, `the sitting day on which the material was presented or made, counting the first sitting day after the instrument was presented as 1` IS A NUMBER, theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheInstrumentWasMade IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142 (2): the material may be considered in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument` MEANS
    IF   NOT theMaterialIsAsTheItemDescribesIt
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER item
         WHEN `item 1: material not forming part of the Act or instrument, contained in an authorised version of it` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `item 2: a relevant report of a royal commission, law reform commission, committee of inquiry or other similar entity` THEN
             IF   theInstrumentWasPresentedToTheAssembly
             THEN
                 IF   `the sitting day on which the material was presented or made, counting the first sitting day after the instrument was presented as 1` AT MOST 6
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE NOTHING
             ELSE
                 IF   theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheInstrumentWasMade
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 3: a relevant report of a committee of the Legislative Assembly` THEN
             IF   theInstrumentWasPresentedToTheAssembly
             THEN
                 IF   `the sitting day on which the material was presented or made, counting the first sitting day after the instrument was presented as 1` AT MOST 6
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE NOTHING
             ELSE
                 IF   theMaterialWasPresentedOrMadeBeforeTheInstrumentWasMade
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 4: an explanatory statement, or other relevant document` THEN
             IF   theInstrumentWasPresentedToTheAssembly AND `the sitting day on which the material was presented or made, counting the first sitting day after the instrument was presented as 1` AT MOST 6
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 5: a presentation speech` THEN
             IF   theInstrumentWasPresentedToTheAssemblyByAMemberOfTheAssembly
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 6: official reports of proceedings in the Legislative Assembly` THEN
             IF   theInstrumentWasPresentedToTheAssembly
             THEN JUST TRUE
             ELSE NOTHING
         WHEN `item 7: a relevant treaty or other international agreement to which Australia is a party` THEN JUST TRUE

-- src:1821 | (3) This section does not limit the material that may be considered in working out the meaning of an Act or statutory instrument.
@ref s 142 (3) (src:1821-1821)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 142 (3): this section limits the material that may be considered` MEANS FALSE

-- src:1834 | (1) If a relevant law provides that stated material may or must be considered in working out the meaning of an Act or statutory instrument, that does not by implication prevent other material of the same or similar kind being considered in working out the meaning of the Act or instrument.
@ref s 143 (1) (src:1834-1834)
GIVEN aRelevantLawProvidesThatStatedMaterialMayOrMustBeConsidered IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 143 (1): the provision prevents, by implication, other material of the same or similar kind being considered` MEANS
    IF   aRelevantLawProvidesThatStatedMaterialMayOrMustBeConsidered
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1835 | (2) In this section:
-- src:1836 | relevant law means—
-- src:1837 | (a) in working out the meaning of an Act—the Act or another Act; or
-- src:1838 | (b) in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under an Act—the Act, another Act or the instrument; or
-- src:1839 | (c) in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument—an Act or either instrument.
@ref s 143 (2) (src:1835-1839)
DECLARE `What is being interpreted for s 143` IS ONE OF
    `working out the meaning of an Act`
    `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under an Act`
    `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument`

-- src:1835 | (2) In this section:
-- src:1836 | relevant law means—
-- src:1837 | (a) in working out the meaning of an Act—the Act or another Act; or
-- src:1838 | (b) in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under an Act—the Act, another Act or the instrument; or
-- src:1839 | (c) in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument—an Act or either instrument.
@ref s 143 (2) (src:1835-1839)
DECLARE `Candidate for a relevant law` IS ONE OF
    `the Act or another Act`
    `the statutory instrument whose meaning is being worked out`
    `the statutory instrument under which that instrument was made`

-- src:1836 | relevant law means—
-- src:1837 | (a) in working out the meaning of an Act—the Act or another Act; or
-- src:1838 | (b) in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under an Act—the Act, another Act or the instrument; or
-- src:1839 | (c) in working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument—an Act or either instrument.
@ref s 143 (2), definition of relevant law (src:1836-1839)
GIVEN interpreting IS A `What is being interpreted for s 143`, candidate IS A `Candidate for a relevant law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 143 (2): the candidate is a relevant law` MEANS
    CONSIDER interpreting
    WHEN `working out the meaning of an Act` THEN
        CONSIDER candidate
        WHEN `the Act or another Act` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the statutory instrument whose meaning is being worked out` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `the statutory instrument under which that instrument was made` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under an Act` THEN
        CONSIDER candidate
        WHEN `the Act or another Act` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the statutory instrument whose meaning is being worked out` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the statutory instrument under which that instrument was made` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `working out the meaning of a statutory instrument made under another statutory instrument` THEN
        CONSIDER candidate
        WHEN `the Act or another Act` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the statutory instrument whose meaning is being worked out` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `the statutory instrument under which that instrument was made` THEN TRUE
